Trigger: Always-On
Environment Instructions

Read docs/prd.md before answering any architectural question.
Reason: The Product Requirements Document is the single source of truth for business logic.

Run type checks before declaring a task complete.
Execute npm run build or npx tsc --noEmit to verify type safety.
Reason: Broken types cause production build failures and runtime bugs.

Do not run destructive shell commands.
Never run rm -rf, prisma migrate reset, or git push --force.
Reason: Destructive commands cause irreversible data loss in development and production environments.

Output file changes as complete files or clear unified diffs.
Do not leave comments like "insert remaining code here".
Reason: Incomplete code blocks cause syntax errors when applied to the workspace.

Check for semantic CSS variable use on every UI change.
Search for raw hex codes in touched components.
Reject code that contains raw hex values.
Reason: The design system requires strict token usage across the application.